WEBVTT

00:00:12.780 --> 00:00:15.640
<i>All right, we've got perfect conditions.</i>

00:00:15.640 --> 00:00:17.950
<i>The Forest Cup in Tsurigasaki!</i>

00:00:17.950 --> 00:00:19.470
<i>The beach that's serving as our venue</i>

00:00:19.470 --> 00:00:21.690
<i>has been packed full of people 
since this morning.</i>

00:00:21.690 --> 00:00:23.160
<i>It's overflowing with excitement!</i>

00:00:29.670 --> 00:00:32.290
Everyone, thank you for coming.

00:00:32.290 --> 00:00:36.180
I am the chair of the competition's 
executive committee, Mori William Soichiro.

00:00:36.630 --> 00:00:38.280
This time, the Forest Cup is being held

00:00:38.280 --> 00:00:40.730
in the same place 
as the 2020 world competition,

00:00:40.730 --> 00:00:43.040
here in Tsurigasaki.

00:00:43.040 --> 00:00:45.780
You could call this competition 
a sort of warm-up skirmish.

00:00:45.780 --> 00:00:48.130
These athletes have their eyes 
firmly set on the future,

00:00:48.130 --> 00:00:50.690
and we hope that they will compete 
boldly and with determination.

00:00:53.070 --> 00:00:55.230
Let's have the athletes take the stage.

00:00:55.230 --> 00:00:58.200
Everyone, please give them 
a big round of applause!

00:01:03.700 --> 00:01:06.210
<i>The day of the competition has finally come.</i>

00:01:06.210 --> 00:01:09.710
<i>I'm all fired up and in the best condition!</i>

00:01:09.710 --> 00:01:12.210
Big Brother, and everyone 
else, too, you can do this!

00:01:14.170 --> 00:01:16.030
Masaki-kun! Fight!

00:01:16.030 --> 00:01:17.590
Star of Oarai!

00:01:17.590 --> 00:01:21.850
Yes! I'll bring the winner's cup to Oarai!

00:01:33.090 --> 00:01:36.070
That's the number one 
pick for first place...

00:01:36.070 --> 00:01:37.860
Fuke Rindo.

00:01:37.860 --> 00:01:40.850
What techniques will he show us this time?

00:01:40.850 --> 00:01:42.380
I can't wait to see!

00:01:46.370 --> 00:01:49.300
<i>I can finally go up against Fuke-san!</i>

00:01:50.610 --> 00:01:52.260
<i>I'm way too happy!</i>

00:02:06.270 --> 00:02:10.900
Let's Go Surfing!!

00:03:23.630 --> 00:03:26.450
<i>In this competition, the main 
competition and the repêchage</i>

00:03:23.680 --> 00:03:29.520
Wave 9    Forest Cup in Tsurigasaki

00:03:26.450 --> 00:03:29.850
<i>will be held simultaneously, 
a double elimination system.</i>

00:03:29.850 --> 00:03:32.180
<i>The time limit is 30 minutes.</i>

00:03:32.180 --> 00:03:35.480
<i>In each round, the top two will 
advance through the main event,</i>

00:03:35.480 --> 00:03:40.390
<i>and the bottom two will move on to compete 
for another chance in the repêchage.</i>

00:03:40.390 --> 00:03:42.740
<i>The two who fight their way 
to the top in each event,</i>

00:03:42.740 --> 00:03:45.380
<i>in other words, a total of four 
will head to the Grand Final</i>

00:03:45.380 --> 00:03:47.240
<i>to compete for the win.</i>

00:03:47.240 --> 00:03:50.730
<i>Ohashi-san! It's finally starting!</i>

00:03:50.730 --> 00:03:54.420
<i>Yes. I'm Ohashi, and 
I'll be providing the commentary.</i>

00:03:54.420 --> 00:03:56.020
<i>I'm looking forward to working with you.</i>

00:04:00.510 --> 00:04:03.010
We managed to get split up pretty well.

00:04:03.010 --> 00:04:04.840
Let's meet at the finals.

00:04:06.760 --> 00:04:10.920
Oh man! I got myself so fired up 
I'm already getting hungry.

00:04:10.920 --> 00:04:12.820
I need an energy charge.

00:04:17.770 --> 00:04:18.650
Hey.

00:04:19.400 --> 00:04:23.090
I'm happy to see you all made it 
safely to the competition.

00:04:23.090 --> 00:04:26.060
And, whatever else is to be said, 
the waves today are magnificent.

00:04:29.030 --> 00:04:31.790
Yeah. These are 
the absolute best conditions!

00:04:31.790 --> 00:04:33.750
It really gets you excited, doesn't it?

00:04:34.110 --> 00:04:35.670
It's a perfect day for surfing!

00:04:36.320 --> 00:04:37.960
A perfect day for Miruru!

00:04:37.960 --> 00:04:42.170
Yeah! Let's enjoy this 
competition to the fullest!

00:04:47.430 --> 00:04:49.360
Catch the wave!

00:04:51.310 --> 00:04:53.670
<i>Now, round 1, heat 1.</i>

00:04:53.680 --> 00:04:56.190
<i>All the athletes are headed out.</i>

00:04:56.600 --> 00:05:00.150
<i>The one to watch is world 
champion, Fuke Rindo.</i>

00:05:00.610 --> 00:05:03.690
<i>Fuke, in red, has already caught a wave.</i>

00:05:05.700 --> 00:05:08.200
<i>He's making full use of the wave's speed.</i>

00:05:15.710 --> 00:05:18.360
<i>He cutback perfectly 
at the edge of the break.</i>

00:05:18.360 --> 00:05:20.760
<i>Now that's what a champion looks like!</i>

00:05:20.760 --> 00:05:23.660
<i>What beautiful, smooth riding!</i>

00:05:31.550 --> 00:05:35.270
<i>First place, Fuke. Second, Kaneko.</i>

00:05:35.270 --> 00:05:38.350
<i>From the start, Fuke 
overwhelmed his opponents.</i>

00:05:39.060 --> 00:05:42.360
<i>And Kosuke and the others 
made it through on solid wins.</i>

00:05:52.000 --> 00:05:53.690
<i>Everyone's getting first...</i>

00:05:53.690 --> 00:05:55.300
<i>They're amazing!</i>

00:05:57.130 --> 00:05:58.980
<i>I've gotta give it my best, too.</i>

00:05:59.730 --> 00:06:03.270
<i>And now, the final heat of round 1.</i>

00:06:04.390 --> 00:06:08.380
<i>The one to watch is the promising 
rookie from Oarai, Hinaoka!</i>

00:06:08.380 --> 00:06:11.260
<i>The source of his energy 
is dried sweet potatoes!</i>

00:06:12.600 --> 00:06:13.760
<i>Okay.</i>

00:06:17.650 --> 00:06:19.650
<i>Hinaoka is really observing his wave.</i>

00:06:20.610 --> 00:06:22.800
<i>He's very high on the wave, 
and he's going long, too.</i>

00:06:23.650 --> 00:06:25.910
<i>I think we can expect 
a high score from this.</i>

00:06:27.070 --> 00:06:31.160
<i>Hinaoka and Watanabe advance to round 2!</i>

00:06:31.160 --> 00:06:32.560
Yes!

00:06:32.560 --> 00:06:34.410
He's made it through the first round.

00:06:34.410 --> 00:06:36.680
That was an amazing floater, wasn't it?

00:06:36.680 --> 00:06:39.000
Masaki-kun has really improved.

00:06:39.000 --> 00:06:40.920
Okay! Just keep it going!

00:06:41.300 --> 00:06:44.420
<i>Next we have round 2, heat 1!</i>

00:06:44.420 --> 00:06:47.420
<i>The one to watch is Matsukaze in white!</i>

00:06:51.750 --> 00:06:54.050
<i>My predictions and 
countermeasures are flawless.</i>

00:06:54.050 --> 00:06:57.320
<i>All that's left is to pick the right 
wave and issue a challenge!</i>

00:06:57.870 --> 00:06:59.870
<i>How long will this Shonan-born thoroughbred</i>

00:06:59.870 --> 00:07:03.060
<i>be able to keep up with world champion Fuke?</i>

00:07:05.720 --> 00:07:08.440
<i>They haven't made a move yet.</i>

00:07:08.970 --> 00:07:11.610
<i>Well, they've got some 
dumping waves mixed in, too,</i>

00:07:11.610 --> 00:07:13.680
<i>so picking the right wave will be difficult.</i>

00:07:17.270 --> 00:07:18.420
<i>Not yet.</i>

00:07:18.420 --> 00:07:20.810
<i>I have to pick a wave with potential.</i>

00:07:22.210 --> 00:07:23.460
Huh?

00:07:44.150 --> 00:07:46.900
<i>He's through!</i>

00:07:48.820 --> 00:07:51.110
<i>This is really amazing.</i>

00:07:51.530 --> 00:07:54.090
<i>His challenging that wave 
defies common sense!</i>

00:07:54.090 --> 00:07:55.060
<i>Yes.</i>

00:07:55.060 --> 00:07:58.060
<i>A surfer's ride is judged on things 
like its aggressiveness, difficulty,</i>

00:07:58.060 --> 00:08:00.430
<i>and whether or not it's innovative,</i>

00:08:00.430 --> 00:08:03.190
<i>but in Fuke's case, he really 
is unsurpassed in every area.</i>

00:08:03.190 --> 00:08:04.790
<i>He's really magnificent.</i>

00:08:09.670 --> 00:08:12.140
The fact that he can ride that is amazing!

00:08:12.140 --> 00:08:14.510
He's able to skillfully ride any wave...

00:08:14.510 --> 00:08:16.180
Fuke-san lives up to his hype!

00:08:16.780 --> 00:08:19.930
Matsukaze, don't panic.

00:08:19.930 --> 00:08:22.570
<i>There are less than ten minutes left.</i>

00:08:22.570 --> 00:08:25.560
<i>Priority goes to Matsukaze in white.</i>

00:08:25.560 --> 00:08:29.940
<i>He's currently in third and needs 
5.1 points to turn it around!</i>

00:08:36.950 --> 00:08:39.440
<i>The predicted potential is 50 percent.</i>

00:08:39.890 --> 00:08:41.350
<i>I'll wager everything on this one!</i>

00:08:55.620 --> 00:08:58.020
<i>Oh. The wave didn't keep running.</i>

00:08:59.140 --> 00:09:03.190
<i>Advancing to round 3 
will be Fuke and Murata!</i>

00:09:05.680 --> 00:09:07.410
Yuta, good work out there.

00:09:07.410 --> 00:09:11.000
While I was waiting for the ideal 
wave, I missed my chance.

00:09:12.170 --> 00:09:14.610
My read of the data 
is still sorely inadequate.

00:09:16.110 --> 00:09:19.120
<i>Moving on, we have round 2, heat 2.</i>

00:09:19.120 --> 00:09:22.300
<i>The one to watch here is Iwana, 
whose home base is Shonan,</i>

00:09:22.300 --> 00:09:24.620
<i>and the organizer of this competition, Mori!</i>

00:09:28.420 --> 00:09:29.610
<i>Very nice.</i>

00:09:29.610 --> 00:09:32.880
<i>His riding is passionate, 
and he's boldly coming in hard.</i>

00:09:35.510 --> 00:09:38.430
<i>Such beautiful, polished action.</i>

00:09:38.430 --> 00:09:40.640
<i>That's Mori William for you!</i>

00:09:44.060 --> 00:09:47.080
<i>In heat 2, coming in first place is Iwana!</i>

00:09:47.080 --> 00:09:49.220
<i>In second is Watanabe.</i>

00:09:49.220 --> 00:09:51.650
<i>And Mori takes a very close third!</i>

00:09:52.090 --> 00:09:54.810
I don't think I lost 
in terms of heart, but...

00:09:55.150 --> 00:09:57.660
I'll aim for another chance 
in the repêchage.

00:09:58.660 --> 00:10:01.810
<i>Now, round 2, the final heat!</i>

00:10:01.810 --> 00:10:04.560
<i>The one to keep an eye on is Kido from Oita!</i>

00:10:04.560 --> 00:10:08.170
<i>Breaking through the dimensional walls... 
What skills will he show us?</i>

00:10:08.560 --> 00:10:11.920
<i>I'm hoping for big things from 
Hinaoka's dried sweet potato power, too.</i>

00:10:12.290 --> 00:10:16.420
Miruru... Right now, 
the two of us will become one.

00:10:19.550 --> 00:10:21.430
This time, I will beat Naoya...

00:10:21.430 --> 00:10:24.010
No! I'll beat the two of them together!

00:10:29.100 --> 00:10:32.620
<i>Kido is working that lip 
with height and power!</i>

00:10:32.620 --> 00:10:34.570
<i>He's making that spray fly!</i>

00:10:35.100 --> 00:10:36.940
Become a weapon, Généroité!

00:10:36.940 --> 00:10:40.640
Miruru and I, together, Bon Vivant!

00:10:47.230 --> 00:10:51.330
<i>Kido and Hinaoka advance to round 3!</i>

00:10:51.910 --> 00:10:53.340
He did it!

00:10:54.160 --> 00:10:58.320
You don't think the others got tripped up 
by the names of Naoya-san's moves...

00:11:00.830 --> 00:11:02.010
It's possible.

00:11:03.030 --> 00:11:07.010
<i>After that, Bill and Yuta, who'd been 
eliminated from the main event,</i>

00:11:07.010 --> 00:11:08.810
<i>moved over to the repêchage event.</i>

00:11:09.680 --> 00:11:17.800
<i>Moving on to round 3 were Fuke, 
Kosuke, Naoya, Watanabe, Murata...</i>

00:11:18.300 --> 00:11:19.760
<i>and me.</i>

00:11:21.130 --> 00:11:22.500
<i>We're finally here.</i>

00:11:22.500 --> 00:11:25.990
<i>In the next heat, I go up against Fuke-san!</i>

00:11:28.490 --> 00:11:31.750
Hooray!

00:11:33.090 --> 00:11:34.900
I'm in heat 2.

00:11:34.900 --> 00:11:36.320
You're competing with me!

00:11:40.490 --> 00:11:43.920
Rindo-kun, you're up against 
Masaki-kun, next, right?

00:11:43.920 --> 00:11:47.510
He's an impressive rookie who 
appeared suddenly, like a comet,

00:11:47.510 --> 00:11:50.310
so there isn't much data, and 
it's hard to anticipate what he'll do.

00:11:50.890 --> 00:11:53.650
He might just be able to call down a storm.

00:11:55.750 --> 00:11:58.720
Where? The weather's perfectly clear.

00:12:06.330 --> 00:12:07.030
Hey.

00:12:10.350 --> 00:12:12.160
It's good to see you again.

00:12:12.160 --> 00:12:14.470
Wow! There's a legend!

00:12:14.470 --> 00:12:15.900
That's Tadao-san!

00:12:15.900 --> 00:12:17.920
What an amazing pairing!

00:12:20.240 --> 00:12:21.800
Yay!

00:12:26.450 --> 00:12:27.590
Fuke-san!

00:12:27.590 --> 00:12:29.730
That was amazing earlier!

00:12:29.730 --> 00:12:30.810
Who are you?

00:12:31.200 --> 00:12:34.690
I'm going up against you next, Fuke-san. 
My name is Hinaoka Masaki.

00:12:34.690 --> 00:12:40.160
I've been super excited wondering 
what kind of battle we might have!

00:12:40.160 --> 00:12:44.130
I started surfing because of a friend 
named Sho that I really admired...

00:12:44.130 --> 00:12:46.450
Oh! Sho's a genius...

00:12:46.450 --> 00:12:49.700
and he could ride any wave 
you threw at him and...

00:12:49.700 --> 00:12:53.210
When I saw you earlier, Fuke-san, 
for some reason you reminded me of Sho!

00:12:53.210 --> 00:12:56.460
Don't compare me to anyone else. I am me.

00:13:01.460 --> 00:13:03.660
Well, that's true.

00:13:03.660 --> 00:13:06.640
It's like, "Who do you 
think you are," right?

00:13:13.640 --> 00:13:14.800
Thanks.

00:13:16.950 --> 00:13:18.730
Yup. I'm fine.

00:13:19.250 --> 00:13:22.240
I'll do my best! I'm going to win!

00:13:24.010 --> 00:13:27.450
<i>Now we start round 3 of the main event!</i>

00:13:27.450 --> 00:13:31.090
<i>Only one from each heat will survive.</i>

00:13:31.090 --> 00:13:32.400
<i>First, we have heat 1.</i>

00:13:32.400 --> 00:13:36.170
<i>Challenging the ultimate champion 
Fuke will be new star Hinaoka</i>

00:13:36.170 --> 00:13:38.210
<i>and veteran Watanabe!</i>

00:13:38.710 --> 00:13:41.090
<i>First, I'll take priority!</i>

00:13:46.570 --> 00:13:48.640
<i>They're going for the wave at the same time.</i>

00:13:48.640 --> 00:13:52.140
<i>Closest to the peak is Hinaoka in white!</i>

00:13:52.570 --> 00:13:54.300
I will take down Fuke-san!

00:13:57.680 --> 00:13:58.980
<i>That's some beautiful carving.</i>

00:13:58.980 --> 00:14:01.530
<i>Oh, but how will this turn out?</i>

00:14:02.490 --> 00:14:04.080
<i>He delivers!</i>

00:14:06.160 --> 00:14:09.990
<i>Usually, you'd lose your balance there. 
He really showed some great control.</i>

00:14:09.990 --> 00:14:14.240
<i>Hinaoka... His innate sense of balance 
is just as the rumors have it!</i>

00:14:14.240 --> 00:14:17.500
<i>He really is captivating to watch!</i>

00:14:19.960 --> 00:14:21.820
<i>Th-That's high!</i>

00:14:21.820 --> 00:14:24.750
<i>It's as though he's going to 
soar right up into the sky!</i>

00:14:25.180 --> 00:14:28.510
<i>With just that one maneuver, 
I'm sure we can expect to see high scores.</i>

00:14:28.510 --> 00:14:32.370
<i>Far and away in first we have Fuke. 
He advances to the finals!</i>

00:14:32.370 --> 00:14:34.420
<i>Watanabe and Hinaoka are headed 
to the repêchage</i>

00:14:34.420 --> 00:14:36.520
<i>to aim for another chance!</i>

00:14:37.310 --> 00:14:40.750
Huh? I... lost?

00:14:42.710 --> 00:14:44.260
Come on, let's get back.

00:14:45.810 --> 00:14:49.280
<i>In round 3, heat 2, we have 
a roundup of powerhouses!</i>

00:14:49.570 --> 00:14:53.530
<i>Which one of them will be 
advancing to the finals?</i>

00:14:59.520 --> 00:15:01.380
<i>In first place, we have Iwana!</i>

00:15:01.380 --> 00:15:03.680
<i>From the main event, 
advancing to the Grand Final</i>

00:15:03.680 --> 00:15:07.160
<i>we have Fuke and Iwana!</i>

00:15:07.160 --> 00:15:09.930
<i>And now, there are only two more 
who will move to the Grand Final.</i>

00:15:09.930 --> 00:15:14.930
<i>First place in each of the heats 
in the repêchage will advance!</i>

00:15:15.330 --> 00:15:18.800
Don't worry, Big Brother! 
You still have a chance!

00:15:18.800 --> 00:15:21.190
Naoya-san, Yuta-san, fight!

00:15:25.400 --> 00:15:27.280
Miruru!

00:15:27.280 --> 00:15:29.900
Revolution Change!

00:15:35.570 --> 00:15:38.060
<i>We've got all the scores from the first run,</i>

00:15:38.060 --> 00:15:40.170
<i>and Kido is in first place!</i>

00:15:40.710 --> 00:15:41.960
<i>Now, for the second run.</i>

00:15:41.960 --> 00:15:46.420
<i>Priority goes to Hinaoka, 
who was the first on the waves.</i>

00:15:49.420 --> 00:15:51.700
<i>Oh! There's Ohara!</i>

00:15:51.700 --> 00:15:54.800
<i>He caught the wave ahead of Hinaoka!</i>

00:15:56.270 --> 00:15:58.310
<i>It has both speed and power.</i>

00:15:58.310 --> 00:15:59.930
<i>He caught a good wave.</i>

00:16:01.430 --> 00:16:04.690
<i>Hinaoka must be feeling pretty frustrated!</i>

00:16:05.150 --> 00:16:05.930
<i>Yes.</i>

00:16:05.930 --> 00:16:09.180
<i>In situations where you need a 
comeback, when you have priority,</i>

00:16:09.180 --> 00:16:11.950
<i>you tend to overanalyze picking a wave.</i>

00:16:12.310 --> 00:16:14.920
<i>He managed three off the lip maneuvers.</i>

00:16:15.370 --> 00:16:17.200
<i>It was a decent ride.</i>

00:16:17.660 --> 00:16:20.200
<i>And now Ohara has taken the top spot!</i>

00:16:20.200 --> 00:16:25.710
<i>Second-place Kido needs 6.6 points 
to turn the tables and take the top spot.</i>

00:16:25.710 --> 00:16:29.090
<i>Third-place Hinaoka needs 8.6 points!</i>

00:16:32.350 --> 00:16:35.060
We have about 4 minutes left...

00:16:35.060 --> 00:16:37.630
I've got nothing left to protect!

00:16:37.630 --> 00:16:39.100
All I can do is attack!

00:16:42.360 --> 00:16:43.910
<i>We've got a set coming in.</i>

00:16:43.910 --> 00:16:45.930
<i>Hinaoka in red is making his move!</i>

00:16:49.090 --> 00:16:50.610
Let's go!

00:16:54.860 --> 00:16:58.140
<i>Oh! To wipe out here!</i>

00:17:01.750 --> 00:17:03.200
Blast it...

00:17:04.250 --> 00:17:06.570
<i>He was aiming for the risky 
lip near the power zone,</i>

00:17:06.570 --> 00:17:08.640
<i>but his timing was a little off.</i>

00:17:09.130 --> 00:17:11.740
<i>However, his assertiveness was impressive.</i>

00:17:12.710 --> 00:17:18.890
<i>Repêchage, round 5, heat 1, the one advancing 
to the Grand Final will be Ohara.</i>

00:17:19.600 --> 00:17:20.960
It's over.

00:17:22.680 --> 00:17:26.120
Great! He pushed himself right to the end.

00:17:26.540 --> 00:17:28.150
Yes, he did.

00:17:28.760 --> 00:17:32.650
<i>After that, Yuta fought a brave fight, too, 
but he ended in second place.</i>

00:17:32.650 --> 00:17:36.780
<i>We didn't manage to make it 
to the finals from the repêchage.</i>

00:17:37.190 --> 00:17:39.910
<i>Forest Cup in Tsurigasaki!</i>

00:17:39.910 --> 00:17:42.660
<i>We have finally arrived at the Grand Final!</i>

00:17:42.660 --> 00:17:46.410
<i>Now, who will be the one 
to grab the glory here?</i>

00:17:46.410 --> 00:17:48.370
<i>Will it be the ultimate champion, Fuke?</i>

00:17:48.370 --> 00:17:50.920
<i>Or, will it be the birth of a new hero?</i>

00:17:56.610 --> 00:17:58.070
Kosuke-san...

00:17:58.070 --> 00:17:59.550
You can do this!

00:18:10.030 --> 00:18:10.970
Here it comes!

00:18:15.530 --> 00:18:18.070
<i>Fuke has caught the wave!</i>

00:18:48.480 --> 00:18:50.640
<i>He's flying!</i>

00:18:50.640 --> 00:18:53.850
<i>That's a rodeo flip! Beautiful!</i>

00:18:53.850 --> 00:18:56.990
<i>There are only a few 
in the world who can make that!</i>

00:18:56.990 --> 00:19:00.970
<i>Fuke delivers a maneuver 
of the highest difficulty!</i>

00:19:00.970 --> 00:19:04.620
<i>How high can the score for this go?</i>

00:19:04.620 --> 00:19:07.370
<i>There it is! A perfect score!</i>

00:19:08.700 --> 00:19:10.050
Wow!

00:19:10.050 --> 00:19:13.880
The speed, the sharpness of 
technique... all of it was perfect!

00:19:16.630 --> 00:19:17.520
Blast it!

00:19:17.520 --> 00:19:20.080
All I can do is give it 
all the power I have!

00:19:21.720 --> 00:19:25.010
<i>Kosuke pushed himself all the way 
to the very end of the time limit!</i>

00:19:27.940 --> 00:19:29.100
<i>In the end...</i>

00:19:30.120 --> 00:19:33.080
<i>The winner is Fuke Rindo!</i>

00:19:36.710 --> 00:19:41.030
Rindo! Rindo! Rindo! Rindo!

00:19:47.930 --> 00:19:51.540
<i>And now the winner's cup 
will be presented to Fuke.</i>

00:19:51.950 --> 00:19:54.120
Congratulations on your win.

00:19:54.980 --> 00:19:56.290
Thank you.

00:20:02.200 --> 00:20:07.430
Fuke, allow me to formally say 
that your riding was truly impressive.

00:20:07.430 --> 00:20:09.400
I think that all the surfers 
you competed with

00:20:09.400 --> 00:20:12.560
feel honored to have had a heat against you.

00:20:12.560 --> 00:20:16.560
Can I ask, is there anyone who 
left a particular impression on you?

00:20:18.930 --> 00:20:21.750
It isn't about beating anyone 
or losing to anyone.

00:20:21.750 --> 00:20:24.320
It's always a battle against 
yourself and the waves.

00:20:24.830 --> 00:20:26.040
<i>Fuke-san...</i>

00:20:26.500 --> 00:20:28.830
<i>He really is super cool!</i>

00:20:29.570 --> 00:20:33.080
<i>Back then, I didn't feel the 
slightest bit upset or frustrated.</i>

00:20:33.720 --> 00:20:35.790
<i>I was just excited, that's all.</i>

00:20:36.210 --> 00:20:37.200
Hey!

00:20:37.200 --> 00:20:39.090
If you've got time 
to gaze in rapture at Fuke,

00:20:39.090 --> 00:20:41.970
then you should do some training 
for the next competition!

00:20:43.800 --> 00:20:47.050
Take that!

00:20:50.910 --> 00:20:53.230
Big Brother! Good work out there!

00:20:53.230 --> 00:20:56.510
Everyone, thank you for cheering me on!

00:20:58.190 --> 00:21:00.110
They were good heats.

00:21:00.110 --> 00:21:02.860
I feel like... you gave me courage.

00:21:04.070 --> 00:21:08.120
Taking one sure step at a time... 
That's what's important.

00:21:08.430 --> 00:21:09.360
Yes, sir!

00:21:17.370 --> 00:21:19.250
We should help, too.

00:21:19.250 --> 00:21:24.510
And do it with thanks to the ocean, 
a feeling of gratitude to the sea.

00:21:25.130 --> 00:21:27.260
A waterman's spirit.

00:21:28.050 --> 00:21:29.850
W-Water...

00:21:29.850 --> 00:21:32.010
Someone who knows the ocean, 
who understands it.

00:21:32.010 --> 00:21:33.330
It isn't just surfers,

00:21:33.330 --> 00:21:38.150
everyone who does water sports 
should aim for that ideal.

00:21:38.760 --> 00:21:41.980
Wow. A waterman, huh?

00:21:55.420 --> 00:21:57.690
<i>The world competition was still very far away.</i>

00:22:02.970 --> 00:22:05.260
<i>I'm sure Sho could do that.</i>

00:22:06.050 --> 00:22:08.930
<i>But one day, I'll fly, too!</i>

00:22:09.380 --> 00:22:12.470
<i>Even higher... even farther!</i>

00:22:14.210 --> 00:22:15.370
Right!

00:22:15.370 --> 00:22:18.380
Starting tomorrow, 
it's back to practicing hard!

00:23:48.940 --> 00:23:54.620
Wave 10
